  "notes": [
   "THIS FILE CONTAINS PROJECTIONS. CBO publishes actuals and baseline projections in one series running to FY2036. _meta.estimate_boundary gives the last ACTUAL fiscal year. No chart may draw actual and projected values as one continuous line.",
   "Fiscal years, not calendar years. FY2025 ran October 2024 to September 2025.",
   "wage_share and profit_share are shares of GDP, not of national income, so they do not sum to 100 with anything. They are comparable to each other over time, not to a factor-share decomposition.",
   "The GDP deflator here is the series used to deflate every nominal dollar figure elsewhere on the site, rebased so FY2025 = 100.",
   "cpi, chained_cpiu, core_cpiu and core_pce are INDEX LEVELS, not inflation rates. A rate is a year-over-year change computed from them; nothing here is pre-differenced.",
   "The price series start in different years, and the gap before each start is null, never zero. core_cpiu begins FY1958 and chained_cpiu begins FY2002 (CBO does not carry the chained CPI-U before then). Each is on its own base, so levels are comparable within a series over time, never across two of them."
